# Design system

Visual and interaction contract for **{{ project_name }}**. App developers and
coding agents treat this file as the generated-project SSOT. The maintainer
wizard (Fraunces, Manrope, federal-blue) is a different product and must not be
copied here.

Register: restrained technical. Prefer tokens over raw hues. Prefer the
commands in [Tooling](#tooling) over ad-hoc checkers.

## Tokens

Canonical CSS variables live in `python/docs/_static/css/design-tokens.css`
when the Sphinx payload is rendered. Framework adapters alias the same hex
values; they do not invent a second brand.

| Role | CSS | Hex | RGB | Notes |
| ---- | --- | --- | --- | ----- |
| Accent | `--accent` | `#14b8a6` | `20 184 166` | Brand teal. Chrome, focus, chart series 0. |
| Accent text | `--accent-text` | `#0f766e` | `15 118 110` | Links and text on `--paper` (AA). |
| Paper | `--paper` | `#f8fafc` | `248 250 252` | Light page background. |
| Surface (light) | `--surface` | `#ffffff` | `255 255 255` | Light raised surface. |
| Text (light) | `--text` | `#0b132b` | `11 19 43` | Light-mode body text only. |
| Muted text | `--text-muted` | `#334155` | `51 65 85` | Secondary copy on paper. |
| Border | `--border` | `#cbd5e1` | `203 213 225` | Hairlines, tables, cards. |
| Hover | `--hover` | `#f1f5f9` | `241 245 249` | Light hover / code wash. |
| Surface (dark) | `--surface` in `.dark` | `#0f172a` | `15 23 42` | Dark surface only — never pair with `--text` `#0b132b`. |
| Surface raised | `--surface-raised` | `#ffffff` / `#1e293b` | — | Light card / dark raised. |
| Text (dark) | `--text` in `.dark` | `#e2e8f0` | `226 232 240` | Dark-mode body text. |
| Paper (dark) | `--paper` in `.dark` | `#020617` | `2 6 23` | Dark page background. |

`--riso-*` names are 1:1 aliases of the unprefixed set (`--riso-accent` =
`--accent`). Keep both in lockstep.

Do **not** substitute:

- Maintainer docs teal `#008080`
- Wizard federal-blue / fluorescent pink
- Infima default blue `#2563eb` / `#3b82f6`
- Per-scaffold Tailwind `blue-*` / `orange-*` / `emerald-*` as the brand

`#14b8a6` on `#ffffff` is below 4.5:1. Use `--text` or `--accent-text` for
copy. Use `--accent` for borders, icons, focus rings, fills with
`--accent-foreground`, and large chrome.

### Light / dark

| Mode | Selector | Paper | Surface | Text |
| ---- | -------- | ----- | ------- | ---- |
| Light | `:root` | `#f8fafc` | `#ffffff` | `#0b132b` |
| Dark | `.dark`, `[data-theme="dark"]` | `#020617` | `#0f172a` | `#e2e8f0` |

Set `color-scheme` on the same nodes. Next.js / Fumadocs / SaaS layouts that
already toggle `.dark` inherit the token swap. Vite, Electron, and Tauri must
define the same pair (or RGB `20 184 166` plus this surface/text pair) in
`theme.extend.colors` / `:root` and `.dark`.

## Typography

| Role | Family | Load |
| ---- | ------ | ---- |
| Sans | **Inter** | `next/font/google` on Next.js surfaces. Self-host `@fontsource/inter` on Vite, Electron, Tauri, and Sphinx so CSP can stay `font-src 'self'`. |
| Mono | **JetBrains Mono** | `next/font` or `@fontsource/jetbrains-mono`. Do not ship Fira Code or Arial as the system mono. |

Do not pull wizard Manrope or Fraunces into generated apps.

Scale (use tokens `--text-body-size` / `--text-body-leading` / `--heading-weight`):

| Element | Size | Line-height | Weight |
| ------- | ---- | ----------- | ------ |
| Body | 16px / `1rem` | 1.5 | 400 |
| Small / meta | 14px | 1.45 | 400 |
| `h3` | 1.25rem | 1.3 | 600 |
| `h2` | 1.5rem | 1.25 | 650 |
| `h1` | 2rem | 1.2 | 700 |
| Code | 0.875em | 1.5 | 400 (mono) |

Letter-spacing on headings: `--heading-letter-spacing` (`-0.02em`). Body color is
`--text`, never `--accent`.

## Color

- Prefer `bg-background` / `text-foreground` / `text-muted-foreground` /
  `bg-primary` (or the CSS variables above) over raw Tailwind palettes.
- Tailwind `theme.extend.colors.accent` / `primary` = `#14b8a6`.
- Electron `--accent` is RGB `20 184 166`, not `59 130 246`.
- Docusaurus `--ifm-color-primary` = `#14b8a6` (not Infima blue).
- Fumadocs `--fd-primary` and shadcn `--primary` map to the same teal, not gray.
- Sphinx Shibuya `accent_color` stays `teal`; content chrome consumes `var(--*)`.

Chart colorway (matplotlib + Plotly + extras):

`#14b8a6`, `#0f172a`, `#0d9488`, `#334155`, `#2dd4bf`, `#64748b`, `#0f766e`, `#94a3b8`

## Motion

| Token | CSS | Value | Use |
| ----- | --- | ----- | --- |
| Color / opacity | `--motion-color` | 150ms ease-out | Hover, focus, theme toggle |
| Transform / layout | `--motion-layout` | 250ms ease-out | Drawers, collapse |
| Enter | `--motion-enter` | 200ms ease-out | Dialogs, toasts |

Honor `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`: drop non-essential animation, keep
opacity/color if a state change would otherwise be invisible. Do not run
confetti or `element.animate()` when that media query matches.

## Accessibility

- Body text contrast ≥ 4.5:1 (`--text` on `--paper` / dark `--text` on `--surface`).
- UI chrome and large text ≥ 3:1.
- Focus: `focus-visible` ring `2px` `--focus-ring`, offset `2px`. Do not use
  `outline-none` without a visible replacement.
- Icon-only controls need an accessible name.
- Color is never the only state signal.
- Mermaid errors use `role="alert"`. In-progress figures use `role="status"`.
- Limit `user-select: none` to drag strips, not document bodies.

## Mermaid

All adapters share one init policy. Never set `securityLevel` to `loose`.

| Option | Value |
| ------ | ----- |
| `startOnLoad` | `false` |
| `securityLevel` | `strict` (HTML encoded, clicks off, SVG run through DOMPurify) |
| `theme` | `base`. Fumadocs retargets `themeVariables` on `.dark`. Docusaurus keeps `theme.dark: 'base'` — do not pair mermaid `dark` with the light token bag. |
| Ids | Deterministic increment (`mermaid-1`…). Not `Math.random()`. Not React `useId()` (colons break Mermaid). |
| `htmlLabels` | `false` |
| `deterministicIds` | `true` |

`themeVariables` (light) map to the token table: `primaryColor` `#14b8a6`,
`primaryTextColor` / `textColor` `#0b132b`, `background` `#f8fafc`,
`mainBkg` `#ffffff`, `lineColor` `#334155`, `fontFamily` Inter. Dark variables
use `#14b8a6`, `#0f172a` / `#1e293b` surfaces, and `#e2e8f0` text.

Diagram padding:

| Kind | Keys |
| ---- | ---- |
| Flowchart | `padding` / `diagramPadding` 16, `nodeSpacing` 50, `rankSpacing` 50 |
| Sequence | `actorMargin` 50, `messageMargin` 40, `boxMargin` 10, `noteMargin` 10 |
| ER | `diagramPadding` 20, `entityPadding` 15, `minEntityWidth` 100 |

`mermaid.render()` SVG may be inserted into the DOM only after `strict`
sanitization. Do not call `bindFunctions` (that re-enables clicks). Do not
recommend unsanitized `innerHTML`.

Implementations (paths are generated-project relative; present when that adapter is rendered):

- Fumadocs: `node/docs/fumadocs/components/mermaid/theme.ts` + `index.tsx` —
  observes `.dark` / `data-theme` and re-inits with the matching token bag.
- Docusaurus: `node/docs/docusaurus/docusaurus.config.ts` (`themeConfig.mermaid`).
  `themeConfig` is JSON-cloned, so one `options.themeVariables` bag (light).
  Complete dark twin: file-local `mermaidThemeByColorMode.dark` in the same
  file. Do not named-export that bag from `docusaurus.config.ts` (Docusaurus 3
  `validateConfig` treats named exports as unknown site-config fields).
- Sphinx: `mermaid_params` `--theme base` plus `mermaid_init_js` in
  `python/docs/conf.py`. Containers stay `background: transparent`.

## Matplotlib

Stylesheet: `python/docs/_static/mpl/riso.mplstyle`.

matplotlib is **not** a default runtime or docs extra. Add it only when the
project actually plots.

```python
from pathlib import Path
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

plt.style.use(Path("python/docs/_static/mpl/riso.mplstyle"))
```

From a Sphinx `conf.py` that already defines `DOCS_DIR`:

```python
from conf import apply_riso_matplotlib_style

apply_riso_matplotlib_style()  # no-op if matplotlib is missing
```

The sheet uses Inter with DejaVu Sans fallback, the chart colorway above,
`--paper` / `--text` / `--border` for figure chrome, and no top/right spines.

Dark figures: set `figure.facecolor` / `axes.facecolor` to `#0f172a` /
`#020617` and `text.color` to `#e2e8f0`. Do not use light `--text` on the dark
surface.

## Plotly

Template: `python/docs/_static/js/riso-plotly-template.json`.

plotly is **not** a default dependency.

```python
import json
from pathlib import Path
import plotly.graph_objects as go
import plotly.io as pio

payload = json.loads(Path("python/docs/_static/js/riso-plotly-template.json").read_text())
pio.templates["riso"] = go.layout.Template(payload)
pio.templates.default = "riso"
```

Or `apply_riso_plotly_template()` in `python/docs/conf.py`. Dark override:
`paper_bgcolor="#0f172a"`, `plot_bgcolor="#020617"`, `font.color="#e2e8f0"`.

